 "text": "Hi, how have you been? Sure. Complementary colors are those that stand out because they' opposite each other on the color wheel. For example, green and red, blue and orange. It matters because it gives your painting depth and character. Using complementary colors gives each color more intensity. Yes, that's right. Green and red, blue and orange, they work well together. You' be surprised how much shadow you can get away with with just a bit of black.",
